        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Perfect! Now I have all the information. Let me compile the answer:\n\n## Summary: ApplicationUser.Enabled and Account Confirmation in Xperience\n\n### 1. **ApplicationUser.Enabled Property** ✓\n\n**File:** `/workspace/resources/repositories/xperience/CMSSolution/Mvc/Kentico.Membership/Stores/Channels/ApplicationUser.cs` (lines 14-18)\n\nThe `Enabled` property is a boolean that:\n- **Represents the lockout notion in ASP.NET Identity** (per documentation)\n- Maps to `MemberInfo.MemberEnabled` (line 67: `Enabled = source.MemberEnabled`)\n- Is bidirectionally synced with the CMS backend (lines 67, 91)\n\n**Crucially:** `Enabled` is NOT mapped to `IsConfirmed` directly. Instead, it's mapped to the **email confirmation status**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **ApplicationUserStore Implementation** ✓\n\n**File:** `/workspace/resources/repositories/xperience/CMSSolution/Mvc/Kentico.Membership/Stores/Channels/ApplicationUserStore.cs` (lines 17-21)\n\n**Does NOT implement `IUserConfirmation<T>`**. Instead, it implements:\n- `IUserPasswordStore<TUser>`\n- `IUserEmailStore<TUser>` ← **This is key**\n- `IUserLoginStore<TUser>`\n- `IUserSecurityStampStore<TUser>`\n\n#### Email Confirmation Methods (lines 491-530):\n```csharp\npublic Task<bool> GetEmailConfirmedAsync(TUser user, CancellationToken cancellationToken)\n{\n    // Returns user.Enabled directly!\n    return Task.FromResult(user.Enabled);  // Line 501\n}\n\npublic Task SetEmailConfirmedAsync(TUser user, bool confirmed, CancellationToken cancellationToken)\n{\n    // Sets user.Enabled to the confirmed status\n    user.Enabled = confirmed;  // Line 525\n    SetSecurityStampInternal(user, Guid.NewGuid().ToString());\n    return Task.CompletedTask;\n}\n```\n\n**Critical Finding:** The `ApplicationUserStore` maps email confirmation directly to the `Enabled` property. When you call `SetEmailConfirmedAsync`, it sets `user.Enabled = confirmed`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **SignIn Flow with RequireConfirmedAccount** ✓\n\n**File:** `/workspace/resources/repositories/xperience/CMSSolution/Admin/Kentico.Xperience.Admin.Base/Authentication/Identity/AdminIdentityExtensions.cs` (line 116)\n\nThe identity system registers:\n```csharp\nservices.TryAddScoped<IUserConfirmation<TUser>, DefaultUserConfirmation<TUser>>();\n```\n\n**DefaultUserConfirmation** (from ASP.NET Identity framework):\n- Uses `IUserEmailStore.GetEmailConfirmedAsync()` to check account confirmation\n- When `options.SignIn.RequireConfirmedAccount = true` is configured, ASP.NET Identity's `SignInManager.PasswordSignInAsync()`:\n  1. Calls `base.PasswordSignInAsync()` (inherited behavior)\n  2. Inside the base implementation, it runs `PreSignInCheck()` which calls `CanSignInAsync()`\n  3. `CanSignInAsync()` calls `IUserConfirmation<TUser>.IsConfirmedAsync()` if required\n  4. `DefaultUserConfirmation.IsConfirmedAsync()` calls `GetEmailConfirmedAsync()` on the user store\n  5. **In Xperience:** `GetEmailConfirmedAsync()` returns `user.Enabled`\n\n**The Chain:**\n```\nSignInManager.PasswordSignInAsync()\n  → base.PasswordSignInAsync() (ASP.NET Identity)\n    → PreSignInCheck()\n      → CanSignInAsync()\n        → IUserConfirmation<T>.IsConfirmedAsync()\n          → DefaultUserConfirmation.IsConfirmedAsync()\n            → IUserEmailStore<T>.GetEmailConfirmedAsync()\n              → ApplicationUserStore.GetEmailConfirmedAsync()\n                → return user.Enabled\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Verification by Tests:**\n\n**File:** `/workspace/resources/repositories/xperience/CMSSolution/Mvc/Tests/Kentico.Membership.Tests/Tests/Stores/Channels/ApplicationUserStoreTests.cs` (lines 278-296)\n\n```csharp\n[Test]\npublic async Task GetEmailConfirmedAsync_EnabledUser_True()\n{\n    var user = new ApplicationUser { Enabled = true };\n    var confirmed = await userStore.GetEmailConfirmedAsync(user, CancellationToken.None);\n    Assert.That(confirmed, Is.EqualTo(true));\n}\n\n[Test]\npublic async Task GetEmailConfirmedAsync_DisabledUser_False()\n{\n    var user = new ApplicationUser { Enabled = false };\n    var confirmed = await userStore.GetEmailConfirmedAsync(user, CancellationToken.None);\n    Assert.That(confirmed, Is.EqualTo(false));\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Answer to Your Questions:**\n\n1. ✅ **ApplicationUser.Enabled** — Maps directly to `MemberInfo.MemberEnabled`. Checked during sign-in via `GetEmailConfirmedAsync()` which returns `user.Enabled`.\n\n2. ✅ **ApplicationUserStore** — Implements `IUserEmailStore<T>` (not `IUserConfirmation<T>`). The `GetEmailConfirmedAsync()` method returns `user.Enabled`.\n\n3. ✅ **RequireConfirmedAccount** — When enabled, ASP.NET Identity's `SignInManager.PasswordSignInAsync()` calls the confirmation chain above, which ultimately checks `ApplicationUser.Enabled` via `GetEmailConfirmedAsync()`. **Disabled accounts (Enabled=false) cannot sign in.**",
