              "arguments": "{\"file_text\": \"# Handoff: DOC-3187 — Migrate registration and authentication code samples to webapp\\n\\n## Task Status\\ncompleted\\n\\n## What Was Accomplished\\n\\nMigrated ~20 substantial inline code blocks from 4 registration/authentication documentation pages into compilable C# files in the CodeSamples project, linked via `{% code_link %}` Liquid tags.\\n\\n### Existing files with Include markers added (7 files):\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/Controllers/AccountController.cs` — Added `signin-get`, `signin-post`, `signout`, `register-get`, `register-post` markers (excluding ShoppingCartService coupling)\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/Models/Account/RegisterViewModel.cs` — Added `registerviewmodel` marker\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/Models/Account/SignInViewModel.cs` — Added `signinviewmodel` marker\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Views/Account/Register.cshtml` — Added `register-view` marker\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Views/Account/SignIn.cshtml` — Added `signin-view` marker\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Views/_ViewImports.cshtml` — Added `viewimports` marker\\n- `src/_code/src/Website/Program.cs` — Added identity/membership config markers\\n\\n### New webapp-integrated files (4 files):\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/Controllers/PasswordResetController.cs` — Full password reset flow with IEmailService\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/Models/Account/PasswordResetViewModels.cs` — Request and reset view models\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/Controllers/EmailConfirmationController.cs` — Registration with email confirmation flow\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/Models/Account/EmailConfirmationRegisterViewModel.cs` — Email confirmation register model\\n\\n### New standalone samples (5 files):\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/StandaloneSamples/ExternalAuthController.cs` — Challenge, callback, sync for external providers\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/StandaloneSamples/ExternalSignInView.cshtml` — Razor view for external auth buttons\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/StandaloneSamples/ExtendedApplicationUser.cs` — Custom member fields with MapFromMemberInfo/MapToMemberInfo\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/StandaloneSamples/MemberListExtender.cs` — PageExtender adding custom column to admin\\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/StandaloneSamples/MemberRetrievalExample.cs` — Member retrieval via UserManager\\n\\n### Documentation pages modified (4 files):\\n- `registration-and-authentication.md` — Replaced inline blocks with code_link tags\\n- `forms-authentication.md` — Replaced ~10 inline blocks with code_link tags\\n- `external-authentication.md` — Replaced ~3 inline blocks with code_link tags\\n- `add-fields-to-member-objects.md` — Replaced 2 inline blocks, fixed ApplicationUserManager → UserManager\\n\\n### API discrepancies fixed:\\n- `ApplicationUserManager<TUser>` → `UserManager<TUser>` (2 occurrences — class does not exist in Xperience source)\\n\\n## What Remains and Why\\nNothing — all phases completed successfully.\\n\\n## Key Decisions Made\\n1. **Reused existing AccountController.cs** with selective `//Include:` markers to hide `ShoppingCartService` coupling — avoids duplicating working sign-in/register logic\\n2. **Integrated password reset and email confirmation** into the webapp flow (not standalone) — these are core features any Xperience app would use\\n3. **Kept external auth as standalone** — requires external provider config (Google, etc.) that shouldn't be baked into the shared webapp\\n4. **Small Program.cs config snippets** (2-5 lines) left inline in docs — extracting adds complexity without value\\n5. **Used `Codesamples.Membership.Standalone` namespace** for standalone samples — matches existing `Codesamples.Commerce.Standalone` convention\\n6. **Supersedes DOC-3186 approach** (PR #3033) which put everything in StandaloneSamples — this task integrates compilable samples into the webapp with proper MVC structure\\n\\n## Source Code References\\n- Claim: \\\"`ApplicationUserManager<TUser>` does not exist\\\" → Verified by researcher — standard `UserManager<T>` from Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity is used instead. [ApplicationUser.cs](https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#Kentico.Membership/ApplicationUser.cs)\\n- Claim: \\\"`MapFromMemberInfo`/`MapToMemberInfo` are virtual methods\\\" → [ApplicationUser.cs](https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#Kentico.Membership/ApplicationUser.cs) — virtual methods available for override\\n- Claim: \\\"`PageExtender<MemberList>` uses composition\\\" → [MemberList](https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#Kentico.Membership/MemberList.cs) is sealed but PageExtender works via composition pattern\\n\\n## Review Status\\nAll three reviewers approved on first pass (no revision cycles needed):\\n- **Technical accuracy**: Approved — all API types, markers, and behavioral claims verified correct\\n- **Style & grammar**: Approved — 3 non-blocking suggestions for minor consistency improvements\\n- **Information architecture**: Approved — code sample migration preserves navigation, cross-references, and content flow\\n\\n## Open Questions Requiring Human Judgment\\n- The 3 non-blocking style suggestions from the style reviewer may warrant minor tweaks at the reviewer's discretion\\n- Verify rendered output of code_link tags on the 4 doc pages matches the original inline code blocks\\n\\n## Pull Request\\n[PR #3034](https://dev.azure.com/KenticoCustomerSuccess/CustomerEducation/_git/kentico-docs-jekyll/pullrequest/3034) (draft)\\n\\n## Suggested Next Steps\\n1. Review the PR diff — 20 files changed (9 new, 11 modified)\\n2. Spot-check rendered code_link output on a few doc pages\\n3. Confirm the Include marker regions in AccountController.cs correctly exclude ShoppingCartService references\\n4. Merge when satisfied\\n\", \"path\": \"/tmp/mcp-attachments/handoff-DOC-3187.md\"}"
